              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                LGXNDS and Transparent Labs both cost $64.99 for 30 servings, which looks like a tie. But Transparent Labs gives 28 g of protein per scoop against 25 g, so LGXNDS costs about 12 to 16% more per gram. Always divide price by servings and protein before you compare.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting the enzymes to fix lactose problems</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The LGXNDS enzyme blend is protease and papain, which digest protein, at a small dose of about 10 mg each. It contains no lactase. If dairy bloats you, the low lactose of the isolate itself is what helps, and any good isolate gives you that.
